              "text": "よういする (yōi suru) is built from a Sino-Japanese noun and the native verb suru, \"to do\". The noun, yōi, is two Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese: yō, \"utilize\" (Middle Chinese yowngH) and i, \"mind\" ('iH) (KANJIDIC2; JMdict; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription)."
